                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "22599674",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197996982753",
                            "num_reviews": 16,
                            "playtime_forever": 30,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "last_played": 1461454602
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Be warned -- this is a \"message\" game, to such an extent that making sure the player gets the message completely and totally overrides any sembelance of story.  While I agree that such themes are important, and I even agree with the positions the game forces you to take, being /forced/ into those positions kinda defeats the purpose of \"Choice Of Games\", doesnt it?\n\nI can't recommend the game because:\n1) If you agree with the postions that the game forces on you, then there is no game.\n2) If you /don't/ agree with the positions that the game forces on you, then you'll find yourself totally unable to express your opinions.\n3) In either case, the game is hardly worth of the title -- it is really more of a quasi-interactive book.\n\nI'm not going into details of the games message because its irrelevant to my recommendations.  I rather suspect that I'll get a dozen comments accusing me of a bigot, so if you /really/ want to know, read the comment thread. :(",
